-
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- The CF method uses a different coordinate convention (width, height vs height, width), requiring a transpose of the output voxels (`voxels.transpose(0, -1)`), which regresses performance [S1, unofficial].
-- The implementation is CPU-only; GPU tensors are automatically moved to CPU for processing and moved back, issuing a warning [S1, unofficial].
-- For the CF method, `filter_radius` must equal half voxel size; otherwise, it has no effect [S1, unofficial].
-- The 'auto' method selects 'cf' if `filter_radius` equals half voxel size, otherwise 'mc' [S1, unofficial].
-- Grid coordinates range from $-1$ to $1$, with cell spacing $\text{step}_x = 2/\text{depth}$, $\text{step}_y = 2/\text{height}$, $\text{step}_z = 2/\text{width}$ [S1, unofficial].
-- Degenerate triangles with area $< 10^{-12}$ are skipped to avoid division by zero [S1, unofficial].
+### Parameters
+*   `num_samples_per_voxel`: Number of samples per voxel for MC forward pass. Default: 16 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `num_samples_per_simplex`: Number of samples per simplex for MC backward pass. Default: 64 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `filter_radius`: Radius of the filter. Default: half_voxel_size. For CF method, it must equal half_voxel_size, otherwise it has no effect [S1, unofficial].
+
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Coordinate Convention:** The CF method uses a different coordinate convention (width, height vs height, width), requiring a transpose of the output voxels (`voxels.transpose(0, -1)`), which regresses performance [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Hardware Support:** The implementation is CPU-only; GPU tensors are automatically moved to CPU for processing and moved back, issuing a warning [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Degenerate Triangles:** Triangles with zero area (normal length < $10^{-12}$) are skipped in the backward pass [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Method Selection:** The 'auto' method selects 'cf' if `filter_radius` equals half_voxel_size, otherwise 'mc' [S1, unofficial].
 
